A||N||16||pherder||Spanked @ car show by brand new cars!!!||||8||
Z||000000||pherder||04-29-2001||02:39 PM||||To forget about things in general (and being laid off in particular), I decided to show the 88 Fiero Coupe w/HO Quad 4 at a local car show.<P>Started off real nice ... the "guards" at the entrance won't let me in ... "this entrance is for show cars, you will have to park somewhere else."  After explaining that this was a show car, I was let in.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I put the car in "Sports" class since NOTHING else came close.  There were 7 cars in the class and 4 of the 7 were BRAND NEW CARS!!!<P>I have been cleaning on the Coupe for several days ... never got it clean enough ... kept finding things that needed cleaning/touchup/etc.<P>Winner of the class ... '01 Prowler!  &lt;1 month old!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>You got money ... you can buy a show winner.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Got the car clean, at least.  Was asked to come to another show today ... didn't want to be abused twice in one weekend.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p6227cceb868c5ee82db7bb8c32555ac7/fe9bf375.jpg.orig.jpg"> <P>Paul||||reg||8
Z||000001||gixxer||04-29-2001||02:53 PM||||Find out who put on the "show", so in the future you can avoid them.<BR>Most reputable clubs and judges make some allowances for the cars' age. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||gixxer||04-29-2001||02:55 PM||||Oh yeah, and tell all the car people you know in your area what you think about it also.||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||04-29-2001||03:29 PM||||I have a 70 Chevelle with 2 455ci engines that took me 5 years and over $20'000 to build.The last show I was in,I was beat by a car that should not have been in the same county as my car,but he belonged to the club that was holding the show.That was over 6 years ago,I haven't shown the car since. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||04-29-2001||05:12 PM||||In the generic car shows, you are apt to be put into any old class that the show sponsors deem appropriate.  Most of those sponsors understand only Corvette, GTO, Camaro or Trans Am.<P>The last generic show I was in, I was put in with 56, 57 T-Bird, Mercedes and Triumph.. the class was 2 seat sport cars.  At least I wasn't in with the Vettes.  Look at is as a chance to check out oter cars.<P>Even some club Fiero meets, it seems that the club members win the trophies when "peer" judging is the thing.  Who said life was fair?||||reg||9
Z||000005||Phil||04-29-2001||06:04 PM||||At nonFiero shows that happens to me all the time, but I go to meet the people, yak and watch my buddy win with his 78 Trans Am||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dave Gunsul||04-29-2001||06:30 PM||||I hate it when new cars win over older cars!<BR>They should be in a new car class but I could<BR>care less about winning a plastic trophy.<BR>If someone comes up to my car and really likes it that's enough for me.<BR>That one person that takes the time to come up to you and tell you in person that he/she<BR>likes your car is worth a lot!<P>BTW I looked at your pic. above and I think<BR>it's a beautiful car!! The guards at the entrance of the car show must have been on crack to not let you in!<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroLisa||04-29-2001||08:59 PM||||Good time for me to do todays car show rant.  I drove down to Cincinatti for a big show today....over 700 cars were there. I was put in the "Open" class since they didn't apparently have anything else to fit me in. In my class was a Mustang Mach 1, a late 60's Mustang convert, a 96 or so Corvette and random other things like that. So I clean my car up and she's lookin real good and I'm happy and I sit through all the awards waiting for them to announce class 28.  Only they didn't judge it. They decided for some reason that the Open class should still pay a $20 entry fee and NOT GET JUDGED. I thought I was going to flip out. I asked the announcer guy why the hell I paid the same money as everyone else and didn;t get a trophy. He said "Its a display class" Hell I don't have to pay to have a few people come tell me they like my car. They had over 700 cars there, $20 a pop, they damn well had enough money to buy 3 more trophies.  I didn't pre-enter for the show and they didn't bother to tell me at registration that my class wasn't judged.<P>GRRRRRRRR.<P>OK I'm done now, and got a car show in Indy next weekend  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||04-29-2001||09:00 PM||||lisa and I went to a big show near cincy today. We both got put in a class called OPEN. ??????? anyway, we cleaned em up and polished then sat or walked around. There were LOTS of cars and talked to lots of people. At the awards at the end our class was not given any. Lisa was PO'd, they told her that cars in the OPEN class were for show only not to compete. No one ever mentioned this when we registered, we kept waiting for judges. They were happy to take our $20 entry though.||||reg||1
