Z||000011||FieroLisa||04-30-2001||12:30 PM||||Harry- the show was put on by the Sharonville City Council or something like that. I'm still mad about that, that $20 entry fee coulda helped me pay for my new brake pads!||||reg||1
Z||000012||BBBAD GT||04-30-2001||02:06 PM||||Last year, I enterd the V8 into a local carshow, judged by the HS autotech class.  The car that won above me was a 1998 Grand Prix GTP, bone stock except he said he had an aftermarket intercooler (which put him in the Custom catagory).  Curious, I go over to look at it, and I couldn't find it.  I asked the owner where it was, and he just pointed to the airfilter box.  Laughing, I said 'where?'  He said he bought it off the internet, and it cools the air going to the motor.  He couldn't understand the air that needs to be cooled is the air that is pushed out by the blower, so he just shook his head and said 'go to this website, it has all the details there'.  What a joke.<P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||2
Z||000013||pontiacs4me||04-30-2001||04:10 PM||||Paul, last summer I entered my firebird in an autozone free car show. (central and tyler)  they gave away door prizes, I got a carb spacer, and they gave small plaques for winning the class.  A there was about 40 cars, and there was like 5 classes.  The show was put on by a local car club, and guess what, the club members won the whole thing.  The car that won the class I was in, was in primer.  WTF?  My car was looking good.  So there was another show awhile back at hometown buffet, I just slowed down a little to check out the cars from central, and blasted off as everyone in the parking lot turned to see what the hell that noise was.  Enough gratification for me.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Alex4mula||04-30-2001||05:33 PM||||And what about when and old car with near 0 miles (trailer/garage queen) wins over one with 100,000+ miles that looks almost the same? How much effort you need to put that 100K+ car to look like new?? If I have had the money to buy one Fiero for every year back in the 80s and stored them in my garage without using them I would be winning lots of trophies in many shows now. I think those should have a category by themself. If I was a judge I would prize effort over money (to buy & not use). But...||||reg||1
